[11:34:50.515] ======================================================================
[11:34:50.515] THE THREE CHAINS (README 九)
[11:34:50.515] ======================================================================
[11:34:50.515] 1) C var -> GCC -> ELF .text/.data/.bss -> ELF loader -> VMA
[11:34:50.515]    -> page table -> MMU -> physical RAM
[11:34:50.515] 2) malloc() -> glibc allocator -> brk/mmap -> demand paging
[11:34:50.515] 3) C pointer -> LOAD/STORE -> MMU -> page fault -> SIGSEGV on error
[11:34:50.515] Not every page fault is a bug: demand paging and COW are normal.
